    "result_text": "All 286 tests pass, including the new `Cp17Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` rule for owner creation: when a new owner is created, the field is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city, otherwise `false` \u2014 creation still succeeds either way.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (so it appears in the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct maps it automatically).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `shares_household` column field with getter/setter.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 computes the flag at creation via a new `sharesHousehold(owner)` helper that case-insensitively matches an existing owner's address and city (mirroring the style of the neighboring `countNamesakes`/`generateCustomerCode` helpers). Computed after city canonicalization so it's consistent with the stored city.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column; the hsqldb seed `data.sql` (the profile used by tests, positional inserts) got a `FALSE` value appended to each owner row.\n\nThe value is persisted at creation and returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`, which is what the test reads back.",
